gin this  might actually be the most comic  accurate episode from marvel studios  that we've gotten so far out of all the  disney plush shows now in the comics  when she first debuts she is much like  when she debuts in episode one she is a  huge fan of superheroes specifically  captain marvel so she's an incredibly  relatable character to all of us because  we are all fans of superheroes now with  the exception of no inhumans or terrigen  mist komala's origin is kind of similar  in the comics except for these bands  which are extremely important and we're  about to get to but in the comics kamala  wants to go to a party against her  parents wishes so against their wishes  she actually goes to the jersey  waterfront unfortunately there she runs  into zoey who of course was introduced  in this episode as well and her  boyfriend josh and they pick on her and  ostracize her miserable she starts to  head home when all of a sudden the city  is clouded in terrigen mist she then  goes unconscious in her terrigen cocoon  where she sees a vision of her three  favorite superheroes captain america  iron man and of course captain marvel  and what's interesting is that in this  vision the heroes actually scold her  they tell her that she's disobedient and  they ask her what she wants in life in  which kamala tells them she wants to be  more like captain marvel a beautiful and  awesome butt-kicking woman who was also  less complicated now when kamala emerges  she has shape-shifting powers and  originally she actually looks like  captain marvel it's also important to  note that in the comics at least kamala  khan also finds out that she has healing  abilities she can heal herself by  reverting back to her normal form but  after the terrigen miss clears and after  kamala calms down after finding out that  she has polymorph abilities she  eventually makes her way back to the  jersey waterfront in which she sees  zoe's drunken boyfriend josh  accidentally cause her to fall into the  