lace now in the comics what the nega  bands do is transform mental energy into  physical energy and based off of the  first episode and what we've seen in the  trailers it sure does seem like that's  what kamala's powers are her thinking  something and then it manifesting  through the power of the bracelet plus  not to mention she does say that the  power feels cosmic and sadly i'm  assuming they're not talking about me  but cosmic energy which is where things  get a little bit more interesting you  see the bands were originally given by  the cree supreme intelligence who we saw  in the first captain marvel film to  captain marvel not captain marvel but  captain mar dash vel however the bands  then trapped him inside of the negative  zone which i believe we actually saw in  this episode as we see kamala puts on  the bracelet and then enters another  type of realm here which does kind of  seem like a negative zone now  fortunately for kamala she does not get  trapped inside but i'm assuming we'll  revisit this soon in a later episode but  i believe that this is how miss marvel  is going to connect to captain marvel in  the mcu the mega bands are extremely  powerful and as i mentioned they are  from the cree and captain marvel isn't  really a cree but hey she thought she  was for a very long time and eventually  in the comics the nega bands were used  to create a nega bomb in which under the  influence of the supreme intelligence  they sent to devastate cree space this  is how i believe miss marvel is going to  draw the attention of captain marvel i  think captain marvel has probably sensed  that somebody has put on the nega bands  if anything captain marvel has sensed  this cosmic energy coming from earth and  i definitely think this series ends with  captain marvel showing up and telling  kamala that perhaps these bands have  drawn some unwanted attention and some  people are coming and that's going to  lead to the events of the marvels so yes  the origin of how kamala khan got her  powers have been changed however her  powers are pretty much similar here  instead of her body simply expanding it  looks more like an energy expansion but  it still looks pretty dang cool and like  i said the series overall has provided  some pretty dang good easter eggs and  some pretty dang comic accurate scenes  for example the scene in the beginning  where we see kamala walk downstairs and  we see her family from the first time is  taken exactly from the comics she walks  down and her brother is praying and her  father says and this is word for word  from the comic amir if you don't stop  praying long enough to put some food in  your mouth one day you will starve to  death in which in the show amir says may  allah forgive you one day and in the  comics he says may allah forgive you abu  in which in arabic abu means father of  so this scene was taken right from the  comics almost word for word exactly  which i personally really love that  combined with all the other awesome  easter eggs like the big little me a  scott lang interview about ant-man  podcast the fact that avengers con is  held at camp lehigh which is the new  jersey base where steve rogers trained  we also saw it in captain america the  winter soldier when natasha and steve  both went back to it then of course in  avengers in-game cap and tony went back  to it in 1970. plus not to mention at  avengers con you see a bunch of  different cosplayers as a bunch of  different superheroes and we do have a  tribute to natasha and tony so overall  in the first episode there were a lot of  really cool things that we saw and i do  think that this band that kamala has is  linked to the crease somehow and that is  how captain marvel comes into kamala  khan's life but let me know your best  theories about this in the comments down  below and let me know what your favorite  easter egg of episode 1 of miss marvel  was don't forget to like the video and  subscribe so you don't miss out on any  of 